      title: "Application for return",
      severity: "",
      maxPenalty: "",
      summary: "Within 60 days of a seizure, finding or acquisition, anyone may apply in writing to a justice (after notifying the Attorney General) for return of a controlled substance, precursor or chemical offence-related property. If the applicant is the lawful owner or lawful possessor and the Attorney General does not say it may be needed for proceedings, the justice orders it returned as soon as practicable. If it may be needed, the order is for return after 180 days if no proceeding has started, or at the conclusion of any proceeding in which the applicant is not found guilty of an offence related to it. If the applicant is not the lawful owner or possessor, and it is not needed, the justice orders it forfeited to the Crown. If it was already disposed of under s. 26, the justice orders payment of its value to an applicant who is the lawful owner or possessor.",
