      summary: "An order under s. 45.1 or 45.2 is reviewed by a review officer other than the person who made it, on the written request of the person ordered, but only on grounds of fact or mixed fact and law. The request must state the grounds and supporting evidence and reach the Minister within seven days of the order being provided. A review is not done if the request does not comply, or is frivolous, vexatious or not in good faith, and the person must be told why in writing. A review officer may also review an order on their own initiative. The order stays in effect during the review unless the review officer decides otherwise. The review must be completed within 30 days of the request reaching the Minister, extendable by up to 30 days at a time with written reasons. The officer may confirm, amend, terminate or cancel the order, and an amended order can be reviewed again.",
